## 3. Confirmed Assumptions and Binding Decisions

The following assumptions have been confirmed and shall be treated as requirements.

| ID | Decision | Consequence / Rule |
|---|---|---|
| A-1 | XP rate is **10 XP per completed 10 minutes**. | The default XP rate is fixed at 10 XP per completed 10-minute block. |
| A-2 | Partial 10-minute blocks award no XP. | Example: 25 minutes awards XP for 20 minutes only. |
| A-3 | Sessions that cross midnight are attributed entirely to the **calendar day on which they started**. | The full duration and XP count toward the start day. Sessions are not split across days. |
| A-4 | Custom session duration minimum is **5 minutes**, maximum is **12 hours**. | Sessions outside this range are rejected with a friendly validation message. |
| A-5 | Default save location is the current user’s application data folder. | The save file is not required to be stored alongside the executable. |
| A-6 | “This week” means **Monday through Sunday**. | Statistics use a local calendar week starting on Monday. |
| A-7 | A streak counts a day only if the user studied for at least **10 minutes** on that day. | Days with less than 10 minutes do not extend or preserve a streak. |
| A-8 | v1 supports deleting sessions but not editing sessions. | Editing may be considered for a future version. |
| A-9 | Manual “Load” replaces the current in-memory data after confirmation. | Loading a file is treated as replacing the current dataset. |
| A-10 | Default theme is **dark mode**. | Dark mode is used on first run unless the user changes it. |
| A-11 | Medal counts in statistics use only the **highest medal earned per day**. | A 5-hour day counts as one Gold day, not Bronze, Silver, and Gold. |
| A-12 | Overlapping sessions are allowed and simply added together. | The application does not need to detect or prevent overlapping study entries. |
| A-13 | The app trusts the local system clock and does not synchronize time. | No network time, timezone correction, or server time validation is required. |

