## 6. Functional Requirements

## 6.1 Study Sessions and XP

| ID | Requirement | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| FR-1 | The application shall allow the user to log a study session using preset durations: 30 minutes, 1 hour, and 2 hours. | Preset logging should be one tap from the Home screen. |
| FR-2 | The application shall allow the user to log a custom duration using hours and minutes. | Custom entry shall open a modal dialog. |
| FR-3 | Custom duration entry shall provide separate fields for hours and minutes. | This is simpler and less error-prone than a single free-text field. |
| FR-4 | Custom duration shall be valid only if total duration is at least 5 minutes and no more than 12 hours. | Values outside this range shall be rejected with a friendly message. |
| FR-5 | Minutes input shall accept values from 0 to 59. | Hours input shall accept values from 0 to 12. |
| FR-6 | When a session is logged, the application shall timestamp it with a start datetime and an end datetime. | The end datetime shall be the current local time at logging. The start datetime shall be end time minus duration. |
| FR-7 | Each session shall be attributed to the calendar day on which its start datetime falls. | This is the confirmed day attribution rule. |
| FR-8 | Sessions that cross midnight shall not be split across calendar days. | The full duration and XP are assigned to the start day. |
| FR-9 | XP shall be awarded at a fixed rate of **10 XP per completed 10 minutes**. | This value shall be configurable as a persisted application setting, but v1 does not require a UI to change it. |
| FR-10 | XP shall be calculated only from completed 10-minute blocks. | Partial blocks shall be rounded down. |
| FR-11 | XP values shall be whole numbers. | No fractional XP shall be displayed or stored. |
| FR-12 | Total session duration shall count toward daily medal thresholds even if the session is too short to earn XP. | Example: a 15-minute session gives 10 XP and counts as 15 minutes toward medals. |
| FR-13 | The application shall allow the user to delete an existing session. | Editing is out of scope for v1. |
| FR-14 | Deleting a session shall require confirmation. | This prevents accidental loss. |
| FR-15 | Deleting a session shall immediately update daily totals, medals, calendar display, statistics, and streaks. | Derived values must not remain stale. |
| FR-16 | The application shall not prevent overlapping sessions. | Overlap validation is not required for v1. |

### XP Calculation Examples

These examples assume the confirmed default rate of 10 XP per completed 10 minutes.

| Session Duration | Completed 10-Minute Blocks | XP Awarded | Notes |
|---:|---:|---:|---|
| 5 minutes | 0 | 0 | Still counts toward medal time. |
| 10 minutes | 1 | 10 | Minimum XP-earning duration. |
| 25 minutes | 2 | 20 | Remaining 5 minutes are ignored for XP. |
| 30 minutes | 3 | 30 | Preset duration. |
| 1 hour | 6 | 60 | Preset duration. |
| 2 hours | 12 | 120 | Preset duration. |
| 2 hours 9 minutes | 12 | 120 | Extra 9 minutes do not create another block. |

### Midnight-Crossing Examples

| Scenario | Attribution Rule |
|---|---|
| User logs a 30-minute session at 00:10. The calculated start time is 23:40 on the previous day. | The full session is attributed to the previous day. |
| User logs a 2-hour session from 23:30 to 01:30. | The full session is attributed to the day on which it started. |
| User logs a 1-hour session at 00:20. The calculated start time is 23:20 on the previous day. | The full session is attributed to the previous day. |

