## 6.2 Daily Medals

| ID | Requirement | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| FR-17 | The application shall award daily medals based on total study time attributed to a calendar day. | Total time is the sum of all sessions attributed to that day. |
| FR-18 | Bronze medal shall require at least 2 hours of study in one day. | 120 minutes. |
| FR-19 | Silver medal shall require at least 3 hours of study in one day. | 180 minutes. |
| FR-20 | Gold medal shall require at least 5 hours of study in one day. | 300 minutes. |
| FR-21 | Medal thresholds shall be inclusive. | Exactly 2 hours earns Bronze; exactly 3 hours earns Silver; exactly 5 hours earns Gold. |
| FR-22 | If a user qualifies for multiple medals on the same day, only the highest earned medal shall be displayed and counted. | Example: 5 hours earns Gold only. |
| FR-23 | Days with less than 2 hours of study shall display no medal. | No participation medal is required for v1. |
| FR-24 | Medal state shall be derived from current session data. | Medals are not independent permanent records in v1. |
| FR-25 | Medals shall be recalculated automatically whenever sessions are added or deleted. | If editing is added later, medals must recalculate after edits too. |
| FR-26 | If a deleted session causes a day to fall below a medal threshold, the medal for that day shall be removed or downgraded automatically. | Calendar and statistics must update. |

