| FR-63 | If manual load is canceled or fails, current data shall remain unchanged. | A friendly error should be shown if the file cannot be used. |
| FR-64 | The application shall maintain at least one backup of the last known good save file. | A simple backup file alongside the default save file is sufficient. |
| FR-65 | The application shall create a backup before overwriting the default save file during risky operations. | Risky operations include manual load and schema migration. |
| FR-66 | If the default save file is missing, the application shall start with empty default data. | This is normal first-run behavior. |
| FR-67 | If the default save file is corrupt, the application shall attempt to load the most recent backup. | If backup load succeeds, the user should be notified in a friendly way. |
