## 11. Proposed Project Structure and Module Breakdown

The project should separate GUI, domain logic, persistence, and utilities. This keeps gamification rules testable and prevents GUI code from becoming responsible for business logic.

| ID | Requirement | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| ARCH-1 | The codebase shall separate GUI, core logic, persistence, and utility modules. | GUI should not contain XP or medal calculation rules directly. |
| ARCH-2 | Core logic shall be usable without GUI dependencies where practical. | This supports unit testing of XP, medals, streaks, and date attribution. |
| ARCH-3 | Persistence shall be isolated from GUI and core logic. | GUI and core should not read/write JSON directly. |
| ARCH-4 | Asset path handling shall be centralized in a utility module. | Ensures consistent behavior in source and frozen executable. |

### Suggested Directory Layout

| Path / Module | Responsibility |
|---|---|
| main entry point | Starts the application and initializes the main window. |
| GUI package | Contains screens, dialogs, navigation, widgets, and theme handling. |
| Core package | Contains session models, XP rules, medal rules, streak rules, and statistics calculations. |
| Persistence package | Handles loading, saving, backup, validation, migration, and schema versioning. |
| Utilities package | Handles resource path resolution, date helpers, friendly error dialogs, and logging helpers. |
| Assets folder | Contains placeholder PNG icons and medal images. |
| Tests folder | Optional unit tests for core logic. |

### Example Module Responsibilities

| Module Area | Example Responsibilities |
|---|---|
| Session logic | Represent a study session, validate duration, determine start/end time. |
| XP engine | Calculate XP from duration using the configured rate and rounding rule. |
| Medal engine | Determine the highest medal earned for a given day. |
| Stats engine | Calculate totals, streaks, averages, and medal counts. |
| Storage service | Read/write JSON, create backups, recover from corruption, migrate schema. |
| Resource helper | Resolve asset paths in development and packaged executable. |
| Screens | Render Home, Calendar, Stats, and Settings UI. |
| Dialogs | Custom session entry, day details, confirmation prompts, error messages. |

